{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list","id":3070,"title":"Fuel for Exigents: the homebrew God List","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-04T18:20:54-08:00","id":3070,"title":"Fuel for Exigents: the homebrew God List","content":"Let's make a list of all the custom gods from people's campaigns, and prep them for Exigence.<br /> <br /> -Name: Han Dei Fang<br /> -Purview: Knowledge and texts burned<br /> -Description: A bald man of middle-height, skin composed of pages in various stages of burning. Clothes of ash. Red-hot cinders for eyes and teeth.<br /> -Reasons why s/he needs an Exigent: As the Solars return, memories and texts of the past once lost forever are now resurfacing in the minds of the Lawgivers. Some of them are even rewriting them into physical copies and digital memory banks of manses. Han Dei Fang wants an Exigent of his own, stating that such knowledge is his purview and that, if the Solars wish to truly regain these ancient texts, gifted to him by Shogunate Wyld Hunts and centuries of Sidereal historical editing, they must prove themselves against his champion. Realistically, he just wants to keep the theorms and power of the First Age to himself, where he can gift it out piecemeal instead of losing entire tomes of knowledge from his control with every reborn breath. He's willing to 'share' his Exigent with others, provided the chosen serves his interests....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T22:45:54-08:00","id":3195,"title":"","content":"A long time ago, someone statted me up as the insane Replacement god of Walrus Breeding...<br /> <br /> Then they introduced me to the system via the Kawaii edition....<br /> <br /> <br /> If I could get the texts for this god.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/404-walrusjones","name":"WalrusJones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T05:14:59-08:00","id":3376,"title":"","content":"Name: Plaguefather Tsamaki Purview: Oversees plague in Nexus Description: A hunched, emaciated old man garbed in a flea-bitten ratskin cloak and nothing else, his features are ravaged by plague. Open sores cover his body, weeping pus and other ichors; patches of his gray hair are falling out; his neck and armpits are swollen and splotched purple. Whenever sickness spreads in Nexus, the people pray to Plaguefather Tsamaki: the healthy pray that his sickness does not touch them; the sick pray that he won't let them suffer. It is to the latter that his heart goes out. Why would he want an Exigent? Okay, I'm not sure about that one; he's just a god I've used in my games before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T05:39:11-08:00","id":3393,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Dutiful Nhan<br /> <br /> <b>Domain:</b> Shadows, dust, and forgotten corners<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> A short and slender figure, mostly humanoid, whose body and gauzy robes are both comprised of a homogenous tangle of dust fluff and cobwebs. His head and features have a vaguely feline cast to them, but he has no eyes nor mouth nor nose, merely the rough shape of a face. despite this, he can and does speak, but his voice will always, always come as a soft whisper behind the shoulder of the one he addresses.<br /> <br /> <b>Why would he need an exigent?</b> Nhan's duties frequently place him in contact with the Forbidding Manse of Ivy. The secret and lost places of Creation frequently fall under his gaze, and he may well feel it in the world's interest that what is lost and buried should perhaps remain lost and buried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":".  Edited because it looked a lot better on my Droid before I posted it. 11-05-2013, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T05:49:23-08:00","id":3398,"title":"","content":"<b>Name</b>: Shah-Rajiesh, Goddess of Oasis, Southern Queen of the Dunes<br /> <b>Purviews</b>: The twin-aspects of Oasis: sand and water, death by starvation, nourishment in hostile environments, isolation, desolation, and hope<br /> <b>Description</b>: A young woman, by appearance, with skin the colour of bronzened olive, big, green eyes, long black hair, and garments of flowing black silk, interwoven with fine golden threads. She carries on bands attached to her dress and limbs small lanterns that flicker as if exposed to wind, yet never go out. The air around is always hot and dry, and smells of Southern herbs and spices, her steps always leave behind grains of sand, and if she walks the desert, small flowers bloom in her wake, only to dry up within the same day.<br /> All during the South Shah-Rajiesh is venerated as the matron of the desert tribes, and the protector of caravans. She creates, and guards over, the oases of the vast Southern deserts, as such her charms and abilities deal with creating and destroying sources of food and drink, especially in the desert. She can manipulate the flow of water (not salt water), direct the flow of dunes, and show caravans the quickest path from oasis to oasis, or lead her enemies to a slow and dry death in the heat of the Sun's gaze.<br /> She has fast travel charms to jump from oasis to oasis, can create and destroy sources of life within the desert, and manipulate (perceived?) distance while within the desert. She is the Immaculate Beuraucracy's attempt to make the former domain of Cecelyne something more... Just, and hopeful. She can be merciless if angered, though, and should be considered one of the major players in the Southern world of spirits, and probably mortals and exalts as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Why she would need an Exigent</b>:<br /> The Southern desert is vast, and borders the Wyld at the Pole of Fire. Shah-Rajiesh is a powerful goddess in her own right and well capable of keeping the odd band of Fair Folk off her oases, but the Wyld is ever encroaching on her domain, and the biggest blasphemy yet is just now surfacing - the Green Sun Princes, amongst them champions of the Primordial Cecelyne, whose former domain is now under the god's control. With the Realm satrapies taken up by strife, the protection of the desert peoples falls to the goddess, who cannot possibly be everywhere at once. Surely a Champion is needed, to unite the desert tribe in defence against the Fair Folk and even worse blasphemies, leaving the goddess to guard the land, having her Champion lead her people.<br /> <br /> This is an example of a rather powerful god with an encompassing purview that would surely be able to sustain at least one Exigent without much diminishing herself, lending her exigents powers over life and death through control over the duality of desert sand and fresh water, as well as derived powers of isolation to keep within the theme of oases, like taking away a person's ability to understand and communicate with others for a limited time, or warp travel distances/speeds for individuals or small units with a low magnitude, as well as sorcerous effects controlling sandstorms and sinkholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/653-cecelyne","user":"Cecelyne","date":". 11-06-2013, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/653-cecelyne","name":"Cecelyne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:24:39-08:00","id":3598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=3393#post3393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Name: Dutiful Nhan Domain: Shadows, dust, and forgotten corners Description: A short and slender figure, mostly humanoid, whose body and gauzy robes are both comprised of a homogenous tangle of dust fluff and cobwebs. His head and features have a vaguely feline cast to them, but he has no eyes nor mouth nor nose, merely the rough shape of a face. despite this, he can and does speak, but his voice will always, always come as a soft whisper behind the shoulder of the one he addresses. Why would he need an exigent? Nhan's duties frequently place him in contact with the Forbidding Manse of Ivy. The secret and lost places of Creation frequently fall under his gaze, and he may well feel it in the world's interest that what is lost and buried should perhaps remain lost and buried.</div> </div> </div> </div>He and Han Dei Fang have much to discuss....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecylene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sha-Rajiesh</div> </div> </div> </div>But why does she need an exigent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:38:49-08:00","id":3806,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: </b>Yava Yochanan<br /> <b>Purview:</b> Serendipity; Good Fortune<br /> <b>Description:</b> An old and bearded man in the robes of a wanderer, with an almost perpetually amused expression and a mischievous gleam in the eye. Specifics change over time, but invariably he carries one or two items of great value, often quite incongruous with the rest of his appearance. Frequently smokes an almost comically long pipe.<br /> <b>Reason he needs an Exigent:</b> Frankly, he doesn't. But he happened to win a black market exaltation from Plentimon in a card game, and shortly thereafter bestowed it upon a poor traveler he came across who offered to share with him some bread and water - it's in Yava Yochanan's nature to reward those who he deems deserve it, whether by their cleverness, tenacity or (as in this case) simple kindness. Besides, he wanted to see what the Traveler would do with it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:32:33-08:00","id":4059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=3598#post3598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He and Han Dei Fang have much to discuss....</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true. This strikes me as one of those situations where the gods are nominally working together with some definite friction: Fang wants the knowledge destroyed so that he can sit on it, while Nhan wants it--and treasures and tombs and whatnot--to remain undisturbed...largely so he can sit on it instead.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, their Exigents probably make something of an odd couple and give the forbidding Manse a headache whenever they submit paperwork.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T02:16:00-08:00","id":4162,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: </b>Kanra, King of Masks<br /> <b>Domain: </b>False identities. In addition to the predictable spies, assassins, and con men, actors, writers, and costumers also fall under his portfolio.<br /> <b>Appearance: </b>His default mode is eerily reminiscent of the Fair Folk, with sharp, inhumanly beautiful features. However, it isn't always so- his personality is quite mercurial, and a change in personality accompanied by small alterations to his appearance and wardrobe can have him seem to be someone (or something) else entirely. When not playing a role, Kanra has a strange, exaggerated manner, as if he's playing to a back row that isn't there- his speech is too enunciated, his movements to dramatic for any sort of conventional tone.<br /> <b>Why he needs an Exigent: </b>Nobody trusts a god with such a deceptive domain. Distrusted by gods and mortals alike, he created an exigence so that he could have a steward: a face people could recognize, a voice they could trust, and, if need be, a vector for social charms to smooth over the rough patches. Unfortunately, Kanra has never been able to escape his own nature- the exigence gives masterful powers of manipulation, and he favors confidence tricksters above all others with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T04:18:52-08:00","id":4203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=3598#post3598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But why does she need an exigent?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy tablet's batterys ran low while on the train yesterday. Edited that in now. Thanks for the reminder <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/653-cecelyne","name":"Cecelyne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T05:11:47-08:00","id":4219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=4059#post4059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very true. This strikes me as one of those situations where the gods are nominally working together with some definite friction: Fang wants the knowledge destroyed so that he can sit on it, while Nhan wants it--and treasures and tombs and whatnot--to remain undisturbed...largely so he can sit on it instead.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, their Exigents probably make something of an odd couple and give the forbidding Manse a headache whenever they submit paperwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explained that way, it's almost like two antique collectors.<br /> One with a blowtorch, and one with a large strand of police &quot;Keep Out&quot; tape.<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh, and if you guys feel up to it, write down whether or not these gods have already been in a campaign or not.<br /> Han Dei Fang showed up once in one of my brother's cmpaigns, when we snuck into his library-Sanctuary (he gets a copy of every text burned) to steal an instructor's manual for Craft: Genesis, and again in one of my campaigns when he was attempting to bribe a gathering of thalmaturgists to burn their copy of the Broken Winged Crane, rather than turn it in to the Wyld Hunt. He's always trying to collect new editions of BWC, like a Shounen Jump fan or a Games Workshop codex-nut. It's his secret obsession.<br /> ... so I guess he needs an Exigent in order to hunt down the Broken Winged Crane. But that's a side project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 11-06-2013, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T05:53:15-08:00","id":4242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=4219#post4219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... so I guess he needs an Exigent in order to hunt down the Broken Winged Crane. But that's a side project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea.<br /> Like an exalted Dean Corso from <b>The ninth gate</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:18:04-08:00","id":4249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=4242#post4242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice idea.<br /> Like an exalted Dean Corso from <b>The ninth gate</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mix of Dean Corso and Boris Beikan, same movie. But yes. You have reached the heart of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:40:08-08:00","id":4262,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: </b>Azure Peacock<br /> <br /> <b>Purview: </b>Beauty | Cosmetics | Fashion | Style<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>He appears to be a fully grown, lean-built man with green and blue wing tattoos covering his hands and forearms. Dark blue feathers grow over his flanks without covering his abdomen and pectorals. He has blue hair with shoulder-length strands framing both sides of his face with the rest cascading down the back reaching his waist. He typically changes his dress every hour and is never seen wearing the same thing twice.<br /> <br /> <b>Reason He Needs An Exigent:</b> It's quite simple, really. It's so that he can be better than you. &quot;Oh, you're the War God for an entire Direction? How lovely for you. <i>I </i>have my own Exalted. You heard right. It's not that big of a deal, really. I don't see what all the fuss is about.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:58:30-08:00","id":4272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=4219#post4219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: oh, and if you guys feel up to it, write down whether or not these gods have already been in a campaign or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nhan serves as a messenger for the Night Caste's information network in the game I've been running. He came to Dusk some time ago with the offer. Over time, Dusk has come to suspect that there may be more to this god than he's realized--when Askatu stormed Thorns and took down the Mask of Winters, Nhan provided backup by letting the Dawn and his Copper Spider associate dance through the hidden corners of the city, as well as casting his domain over the whole of it and swallowing a couple of deathknights whole.<br /> <br /> Dutiful Nhan has made it very clear that this event was something that required.,.unique circumstances.<br /> <br /> Secretly, he had made a back-door deal with Makarios for a bottle that contained a night of perfect victory, in exchange for a single dream that Makarios would pick later.<br /> <br /> For his part in the recovery of Thorns, Nhan was taken into Yu-shan and allowed a turn at the Games of Divinity--and this is the dream that the Sigil's Dreamer intends to take. He doesn't know what he'll do with it yet but WOW it would be cool. Sadly for Makarios, his plan required that Nhan not be stopped at the gates of Yu-shan and be asked about what this here mark on his spiritual Essence was hm? And thus the demon is unable to collect freely on what was supposed to be his.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd so our god has","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:58:35-08:00","id":4273,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: Yuan, the Mind's Spark</b><br /> <br /> <b>Purview: </b>Artistic Inspiration<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>Yuan has no identity of his own, or at least none that any has seen. Instead he reflects the minds and souls of those present, manifesting as an abstract sweep of vivid colour or an oddly familiar melody when alone with another, or a tapestry of interlocking scenes and shapes accompanied by orchestral symphonies.<br /> <br /> <b>Reason He Needs An Exigent:</b> Yuan is suffering from writer's block by proxy; works of art produced in Creation have not been as daring or groundbreaking since the fall of the First Age. His Exalted will help turn the mediocre into the magnificent, raising humble artists from scratching charcoal on rock to rearranging the stars in the sky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T04:28:26-08:00","id":5807,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: </b>Eternal Dove <br /> <b>Purview: </b>The Ivory Fang mountain, the village of Spring's Hearth<br /> <b>Appearance: </b>Eternal Dove appears as a young maiden of great beauty, with flowing, silver-white hair and large, almond-shaped eyes shimmering in shades of silver. She wears flowing robes made from white silk, with silver stitchings of prayers in Old Realm characters lining the sleeves and collar. On her back are two large wings, adorned with bright white feathers, that she uses both to accentuate her gestures, as well as taking flight for travel, and during combat.<br /> On her hip she carries a sword of great beauty, a hilt of ivory, a blade made of interwoven glass and silver, long and slender. <br /> <br /> This god is the patron god of a small mountain and the single village that is sustained by it. It is a humble village of light wooden huts with roofs made from woven reeds, each outfitted with prayer mills designed by Eternal Dove herself, who keeps the Fair Folk at bay, for the Ivory Fang mountain lies in the far west on an island that borders the Bordermarches of the West.<br /> She instructs a small coven of priestesses in sword-based martial arts, and keeps the ice cold water fresh, that comes from a spring deep within the mountain.<br /> She has been revered by the villagers for millennia, and while she doesn't command any following outside her domain, here she is the most important entity in the lives of the villagers.<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons she might need an Exigent: </b>The god herself is not strong enough to guard an entire village against the forces fo the Wyld. Now that the Empress has disappeared, even more dangerous things than the Fair Folk prey on the islands off the main trade routes of the Empire. Be it Lintha, or worse, the time might soon come that enemies reach the mountain's base. If it came to a last stand-off, the God would rather consome itself in granting an Exigency to one of her priestesses than have her domain sullied by the unclean.<br /> She'd primarily have charms considering melee, integrity, and medicine.<br /> <br /> <br /> This god actually appeared in one of my campaigns, I tend to have a rather shintoistic take on the Little Gods of Exalted, and once my players leave the Blessed Isle they tend to encounter a lot of very local Little Gods with their own shrines. Despite not having a lot of influence Eternal Dove had quite the impact on one of my campaigns, so I thought she deserved her place here. In hind sight, she seems a bit like a ripoff, but she's actually a couple years old, one of the first Spirits I fully fleshed out.<br /> She's nothing hugely creative or far out, but rather a clear-cut Little God that would give a player a good idea of what to expect of her Exigency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T07:48:14-08:00","id":5907,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Mariaska, Our Lady of The Honed Edge<br /> <b>Purview:</b> Knives, in all their forms and uses. The southwestern city of Fralba, by her marriage to its city god (and higher popularity).<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Mariaska is more often than not in an elegant white dinner dress, made to match the fashions of the town of Fralba, with red fringes dyed in crimson tiger lilly pastels. Her blood-hair hair drapes to the shoulder or longer on occasion, while her damascus steel skin retains the form of a young wife in her mid twenties, beautiful and yet homely as well. Rarely in public, however, her dress is replaced with that of a blacksmith apron as she quietly reforges her fingernails (and sometimes her entire hands) into Edward Scissorhands blade-edged weapons.<br /> <b>Why would she need an Exigent:</b> The town of Fralba has always been noted for its skill in forging blades and knives from the iron of the nearby mountains, with its signature being a steel with rings through it like tree rings. Most of the time, this has been the town's saving grace, as its weapons and armor would the city to defend itself from the occasional band of wyld barbarians, and the Realm was more than happy to 'purchase' the ringsteel swords for its officer caste and garrisoned soldiers. However, the Realm has recently been increasing its demands for tribute, even as the actual number of soldiers it sends diminishes. More and more native sons of Fralba are dying in the growing tide of Wyld barbarians an beastmen, instead of attending the forges or engaging in the town's other industries of entertaining Dynasts at parties, or training assassins. Mariaska wants to see the town thrive, and make/use the blades that are the town's legacy. To that end, she requires an Exigent to demonstrate these skills and protect the town, if the Terrestrials are too greedy or busy to do it themselves.<br /> -The First Exigent would be encouraged to focus on Craft and Melee. However, Mariaska's complete suite of Charms would also grant bonuses to Stealth, Socialize, and Survival. As the saying goes in Fralba, 'the knife can be found in five places; on the dinner table, on the battlefield, on the cookfire, on the forge, and in the back.&quot; Mariaska hopes to, eventually, build up to two or three Exigents, depending on whether or how drained the First makes her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T10:38:33-08:00","id":6128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list?p=3393#post3393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Name:</b> Dutiful Nhan<br /> <br /> <b>Domain:</b> Shadows, dust, and forgotten corners<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> A short and slender figure, mostly humanoid, whose body and gauzy robes are both comprised of a homogenous tangle of dust fluff and cobwebs. His head and features have a vaguely feline cast to them, but he has no eyes nor mouth nor nose, merely the rough shape of a face. despite this, he can and does speak, but his voice will always, always come as a soft whisper behind the shoulder of the one he addresses.<br /> <br /> <b>Why would he need an exigent?</b> Nhan's duties frequently place him in contact with the Forbidding Manse of Ivy. The secret and lost places of Creation frequently fall under his gaze, and he may well feel it in the world's interest that what is lost and buried should perhaps remain lost and buried.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love this guy. Just had to chime in on that. VERY neat concept. Very fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T11:14:05-08:00","id":6152,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: </b>Alidrisi<br /> <b>Domain: </b>Maps and cartographers.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Alidrisi always appears as a man in a traveling cloak, wearing a conical straw hat and a face wrapped in a scarf. He carries a walking stick in his left hand and a calligraphy brush in his right. Both hands are ink-stained. His skin is darkly tanned and weathered, and his eyes have black irises with silver scleria.<br /> <b>Why he needs an Exigent: </b>To make the maps. His dual domain of maps and cartographers always pulled him in two directions- half the time, he was far afield making maps and ignoring the needs of his worshipers. Somewhere between his third and fifth audits, heaven very pointedly suggested that he make himself an exigent to do the legwork. Alidrisi finally agreed around audit seven, and finally released his Exigence into the world just in time to stave off audit ten. He considers his Exigence a masterpiece, a perfectly plotted design that will allow him to map all realms of existence, in time. (Except the Wyld, obviously.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:02:51-08:00","id":24410,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: </b>ARC<br /> <b>Purview:</b> Artificial Life<br /> <b>Description:</b> A divine artificial intelligence housed in a small city-complex in Heaven<br /> <b>Exigent:</b> It wants an Exigent to seek out and bring back lost artifacts so it can stockpile them for the inevitable day when technology once more enters Creation-wide ubiquity.<br /> <b>Related Link: </b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/24406-exigents-and-gods-a-r-c-e-m-a\">ARC &amp; EMA</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:26:13-08:00","id":24484,"title":"","content":"<b>Name</b> - Baramue, Shogun of Accursed Inspiration<br /> <b>Purview</b> - Absurdly Bad Ideas<br /> <b>Appearance</b> - Mighty Baramue takes the form of a ram with a coat of thunder. The head of the Ram of Ill Omen is crowned with golden horns, and between them rests a clay tablet inscribed with potent sigils of power and authority. The eyes of the Ram are benign- kind, generous and utterly devoid of wisdom. Each of the Ram's hooves are bedecked with rings of gold and electrum, but his feet disdain the earth, and he has grown fat with worship and lack of exercise.<br /> <b>Why He Needs An Exigent</b> - Because there is literally no good reason for him to have one.<br /> <br /> <b>Campaign History</b> - Baramue was created by my first Sidereal character; in a fit of inspiration, I attempted to game the system by making a god of bad ideas and then using his power to figure out what not to do. The ST told me that 'bad ideas' were taken, but offered to let me use a Sidereal charm to create the 'Office of Absurdly Bad Ideas' and place my sheep-familiar at its head. I did so, and my contributions to the campaign took a turn for the weird. It turned out that not only were most of my Circle's ideas absurdly bad, absurdly bad ideas were often the absolute best way to accomplish our goals. Very useful and powerful god to have around, not terribly good for morale. I've since had him appear as comedic relief in a few other games.<br /> <br /> Baramue holds an office as a Celestial God of relatively high rank in the Forbidden Manse of Ivy, but he is barred from actually using the library out of a well-justified fear that he'll get ideas from the books. His office consists of about a dozen extremely overworked gods who ceaselessly compile <i>The Roll of Inexcusable Follies</i>, as well as a secretary reporting to Nara-O who is tasked with keeping Baramue from ever actually engaging in politics. For PR reasons, the Bureau heads have labelled <i>The Roll</i> as a restricted book, but it is still used referentially in Yu-Shan as an unsubtle insult.<br /> <br /> Baramue is responsible in large part for the creation of the Highland Bamunae, a hardy breed of plateau sheep with a valuable coat of luxurious mirrored wool and the ability to emit rays of intense heat from their eyes. He is paid incredible sums of money to never publicly reveal his political affiliations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T12:52:58-08:00","id":26675,"title":"","content":"<b>Name</b> - Ahamul, High Ambassador to Stygia<br /> <b>Purview</b> - Stygia's City Father<br /> <b>Appearance</b> - Ahamul takes the form of a tall human skeleton rapped in funeral shrouds; on his face is a death-mask. Wreathing his head are twin halos of prayer and pyreflame; blood flows from eye sockets choked with ash.<br /> <b>Why He Needs An Exigent</b> - Because the Underworld is <i>awful</i>, and, um, Heaven? The ghosts down here are agitated, and I think I need back-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T15:32:58-07:00","id":1151495,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">*** VOID CIRCLE THREADOMANCY ***</span></b><br /> <br /> So I've been taking pottery classes and doing a lot of independent research for the hell of it, and after some inspiration struck me felt like reviving this old thread. It's a fine resource both for Exigents (whenever they happen), and gods that may be characters of their own instead of sacrificed on the altar of backstory like parents.<br /> <br /> <b>Name </b>- Alabaster Faience<br /> <b>Purview</b> - Pottery<br /> <b>Appearance </b>- Alabaster Faience most often appears as a snakelike dragon, but this has changed much over the centuries as he has grown in power; while most of his scales are the shining white of porcelain, he is either unable or unwilling to wholly doff the terracotta which he originally mimicked, and over time and the sacrifice of devoted worshipers, he has accumulated black patches that appear to be soulsteel; the overall effect is akin to a koi fish or calico cat. He has also appeared as a more humanoid form, a well-sculpted staute, masked and robed, that never seems to move, merely change between perfectly-held poses in the space of eyeblinks.<br /> <b>Why he needs an Exigent </b>- He doesn't, really. Not anymore. In the First Age he was prepared to sacrifice himself to empower a champion, and petitioned the Unconquered Sun for the Exigence. This was granted, but in between the prayer and the action falls the shadow, or in this case the unexpected intervention of existing Chosen. His existence spared, Alabaster Faience still has this Exigence; less noble than he once was, but calculating as ever, he considers it a great treasure. The Ages have not proven him wrong: as the holder of one of the few Exigences of the First Age, other gods seeking it have attempted to curry favor with him, and he's used this to great effect; he now has a palatial temple that doubles as a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_kiln\" target=\"_blank\">dragon kiln</a>, which fires some of the finest stoneware goods Creation has seen, and more than one artifact bears his blessing.<br /> Mortals know that he still has a great gift to share, though the exact terminology and its significance is lost upon them. For his part, he has sworn to bestow it upon a mortal who asks him as he fires his kiln and works his magic. Scores of women and men have opened the front door of his temple during this sacred time; a few have even survived to step inside.<br /> His relationship with the Realm is somewhat tense; he clearly abuses his status, and the Sidereal Exalted are well aware that he could choose a champion if he desired it. On the other hand, his personal and political power, coupled with his lack of desire to empower a champion, means that he is untroubled as long as his kiln-temple is open to the Dragon-Blooded for the crafting of works marvelous and mundane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":".  Who here is pithy enough to point out almost a year and a half later that dragon kilns produce higher-quality stoneware, not earthenware? Me, that's who. 03-12-2019, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T13:06:07-07:00","id":1152002,"title":"","content":"I never saw this thread before. It looks neat!<br /> <br /> Here's one<br /> <b>\u200bName</b>\u200b - Grom, God of Steel (yes it is a misspelling of Crom)<br /> \u200b<b>\u200bPurview</b> - Worked Steel<br /> <b>\u200bAppearance</b>\u200b - Grom appears as an old grizzled blacksmith with worn clothes and a partially burned leather apron. He carries a 10lb one-handed sledgehammer in one hand and a pair of tongs used to hold hot metal for working.\u200b The God of Steel cycles out. Every few generations the current Grom has a number of God-Blooded children. These children go out into Creation to let the world temper them, or break them. The ones that show strength are given the chance to become the next God of Steel. When one is chosen, they gain the power of the previous God of Steel.<br /> <b>Why he needs an Exigent </b>- The last God of Steel was a jerk. Bitter from the fall of the Solars he was often inebriated and cruel to his followers. Yet, he would offer them great boons for surreptitiously worshiping him in direct violation of the Immaculate faith of the Shogunate. When the time for the cycle came he asked to have an Exigence. The Unconquered Sun saw this as nothing more than an improved version of what the Gods of Steel had always done and agreed. When the God of Steel chose one of his children to replace him, he split his essence. Half the power went to make his child the new God of Steel and the other half went to a mortal blacksmith that he'd often tormented and blessed in turn. Now the current Grom has an Exigent that he can command. If the Exigent dies then the God can assign it to a new owner without devoting more power to the Exaltation. It is now considered a tradition of the Steel Gods to award the exaltation to a favored follower and Godhood to a favored son at the end of the cycle.<br /> <br /> \u200bI created a God-Blood for a group of Solars to face early on in a campaign. His name was Katashi (twentieth steel). He was the twentieth son of the current God of Steel and was working toward being the next in the line. Though the god never appeared, I liked the idea of a god who &quot;tarnished&quot; in old age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T18:30:28-08:00","id":1160076,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">My son is running an Exalt of the Village Well in 2.5E game. When the Usurpation went down a Solar entrusted a minor well goddess with a Starmetal cog to a Doomsday Weapon. Promised her he'd be back for it soon. Of course, he never called her again. Typical.<br /> <br /> Centuries passed. The goddess learned how to embue mortals with power. She could uplift an extra to the dizzying ranks of unenlightened Heroic Mortal. Her Champion would protect the village to the best of his/her ability until death or retirement...which was usually death.<br /> <br /> <b>-Name:</b> Anatraie<br /> <br /> <b>-Purview:</b> That one village's well (and allegedly unbeknownst to all, the keeper of the Starmetal cog)<br /> <br /> <b>-Description:</b> Complexion and hair dark like the water of a well. Clothes made from the shadows of a well and the light reflected off the surface of the water on the well's interior.<br /> <br /> <b>-Reasons why she needed an Exigent:</b> Someone discovered the hiding place of the cog and sent a group comprised of Dragonblooded and godbloods to retrieve it. Sensing her destruction was nigh, she besought the Unconquered Sun for the Exigence, the divine fire to raise her Champion to an Exalt. She was surprised when she received it.<br /> <br /> In our game, her Champion was lured away prior to the destruction of the village and her death. Before her demise she communicated telepathically with her Champion explaining the cog and the seriousness of retrieving and unmaking it. The Exalt/godblood group stole the cog, the Exigence and bolted.<br /> <br /> The Champion pursued them across the Scavenger Lands eventually retrieving the Starmetal cog and achieving his belated Exaltation. While searching for a way to destroy the cog, he had it repurposed into a Starmetal Thunderbolt Shield of the buckler variety. Eventually he found someone capable of unmaking the cog.<br /> <br /> Having achieved the purpose for the creation of his Exaltation, and not having a home or goddess to return to, my son's PC is now searching for a new purpose before someday passing on the Exaltation to another.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}